          "heading": "Ireland 'A' squad to face Fiji, with Tadhg Furlong cleared to play",
          "body": "Ireland's 'A' side are set to face Fiji, a fixture flagged alongside news that Tadhg Furlong is cleared to play. Furlong also avoided a ban after a 'unanimous' Disciplinary Committee decision over an alleged testicle grab. For Fiji, the Ireland match is a reminder that the Jake White era has a busy November, with Fiji having beaten Japan 34-28 last weekend and facing France, Ireland and Italy in the upcoming Tests."
