      "edition": "Sunday 1 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Test window",
          "heading": "Quesada calls November's four Tests one of Italy's most demanding challenges",
          "body": "Gonzalo Quesada has framed Italy's November block as one of the most demanding challenges in the national team's history: four consecutive Tests against sides he says are all among the world's top ten, starting with South Africa in Turin, then Argentina in Genoa and Fiji in Udine before the final leg in London. He sees it as a test of the group's character, and says Italy must impose their own rugby rather than imitate others. Seventeen players are unavailable."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Argentina lose Thomas Gallo and Santiago Carreras to long-term injuries",
