          "kicker": "Union move",
          "heading": "WRU expresses interest in sending two Welsh clubs into English Premiership",
          "body": "WalesOnline reports the WRU has expressed interest in two Welsh clubs joining the Gallagher Premiership, with talks under way with the RFU and Premiership Rugby. A move could come as early as next season, though the following campaign is seen as more realistic. The WRU still insists it is committed to four URC teams until 2027/28, but a letter to Swansea Council speaks of 'ongoing confidential developments'. With the Ospreys and Scarlets still battling to survive, the summit in December could revisit the four-club model."
        },
