          "kicker": "Opinion, January",
          "heading": "Roar column said Wallabies 'well and truly stuck' in second tier",
          "body": "A January column from The Roar asked whether Australia is ready for the biggest World Cup ever, arguing the Wallabies are 'well and truly stuck in second tier of teams'. It also questioned whether a 24-team tournament risks diluting quality. The question still hangs over next year's home World Cup, and Australia still need an answer at No. 10: coach Les Kiss, who has just recalled Kurtley Beale, says he will reassess the position after the next Super Rugby Pacific season."
        },
