          "kicker": "Tactical analysis",
          "heading": "Japan's new kick-catch tactic is now being countered, analysis argues",
          "body": "Japan have used a new kick-catch method since the start of this year, with player B rather than player A taking the high ball, an analysis published on Thursday argues. The writer says it significantly reduces the risk of penalties for escorting, where penalties have become stricter. The downside is that the catcher must run backwards with support only from player A, and opponents are already countering it. The writer says the kick-catching issue was also highlighted in the Fiji match."
        },
